nt  to take in their laboratory so this  chart is an example of a report that  allows the comparison of multi multiple  levey-jennings plots at the same time  and well this example is showing  different controls so the top panel is a  serie care positive control the middle  panel are the applicant roles and the  bottom panel is the echo metrics control  you can really use a variety of  different combinations of things and and  where I see this being of most value is  in a situation where like our lab where  we have multiple mm mm instruments where  where we are running the same assays and  if you have controls that are being run  on the same instruments for example an  external control and each run the same  external control is being run on  different instruments you can track how  those controls are performing on each  instrument so you can associate one  control with a particular instrument  when you set it up and then generate  plots to compare those the performance  of those and see if there are any trends  that may be instrument 2 is showing some  diminishing values over time and while  they're still in range the use you're  seeing this trend and unless you had  those controls being run on multiple  instruments and you had a good way of  tracking it you might not actually  recognize that  another important aspect of the  functionality of this system is shown  here with this data review report this  allows you to review data for a  particular control over time so this in  this example you're looking at the  bio-rad control level one level two and  level three and this was exactly the  data that I showed you at the beginning  that had all the flags and I just  printed out or took a screenshot of that  report you can see the first one was  rejected and the third run was rejected  in this you have documentation here of  not only the values that were obtained  the action that had to happen as a  result of the rejection so in this case  the test or assay was repeated